(How this report is worked out) Tj
0.078 0.129 0.239 rg
/F2 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 201 Tm
(Fits. ) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 201 Tm
(A resource's fit is direct when an offering of the target serves its taxonomy category and offers every capability the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 189 Tm
(resource uses, partial when the offering serving the category lacks some of them, and none when no offering serves the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 177 Tm
(category or the resource is not classified.) Tj
/F2 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 162 Tm
(Best offering. ) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 111 162 Tm
(Every offering that serves the category is a candidate. Candidates are ordered direct before partial, then by ) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 150 Tm
(how few capabilities they lack, then by name; the first is the best offering. A tie names the other candidates with the same fit ) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 138 Tm
(and as many missing capabilities, which would serve as well.) Tj
/F2 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 123 Tm
(Required changes and blockers. ) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 192 123 Tm
(A required change is a capability the resource uses that its best offering does not offer: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 111 Tm
(the resource moves once it no longer depends on it. A blocker is a resource with fit none: nothing in the catalog serves it. A ) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 99 Tm
(resource that depends on or is a replica of a blocked resource is affected by a blocker on it; the note is not transitive.) Tj
/F2 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 84 Tm
(Workloads. ) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 102 84 Tm
(Resources are grouped by the workload the inventory names, and those that name none form the No workload ) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 72 Tm
(group. A workload's counts and blockers are those of its resources.) Tj
0.290 0.333 0.408 rg
